kosha joint-space

  -- the configuration space of a kinematic chain
  -- each dimension is one kona (joint angle) — the chala-apeksha of that joint
  -- a point in joint-space fully determines the pose of the entire chain via FK
  -- IK is the inverse: find the joint-space point that places the end-effector at target

  "domain-robotics-sthita"

  -- akasham: the space itself; aayaama: the dimensionality (one per joint kona)
  "akasham-swarupa kona-yukta chala-apeksha-sthita"
  "aayaama-vistara-yukta"
  "kinematic-chain-abheda vector-space-abheda"
  "fk-ahara ik-phala"

